[stderr] ## Scope and dependency conclusions
[stderr] 
[stderr] The minimal offline campaign depends on the shell, exploration, narrative,
[stderr] quests/progression, combat, inventory, persistence, rendering/input,
[stderr] accessibility, original assets, content tooling, and quality disciplines. PWA
[stderr] packaging adds installability, caches, offline assets, and update safety; it
[stderr] does not create a separate game.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Account, multiplayer, live-service, and commerce must not become dependencies
[stderr] of the offline campaign until a human resolves their contradiction. If approved,
[stderr] they require explicit degraded states, privacy/security rules, operational
[stderr] ownership, and recovery behavior. If deferred, their interfaces and data model
[stderr] must not expand or block the first release.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Explicit requests, safe assumptions, and approval gates
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Kind | Discovery conclusion | Handling |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Explicit requests | Small 2D single-player RPG; web/PWA; exploration, town, dungeon, combat, inventory, quests, saves, settings, ending, access, feedback, recovery. | Plan as the complete offline campaign. |
[stderr] | Necessary implied capabilities | Shell/session, authored content/tooling, input/rendering, QA, release/update workflow, and balance. | Include in later contracts as enabling work, sized to the small release. |
[stderr] | Safe assumptions | Original content; shared core; durable confirmed local saves when storage permits; connected features visibly degrade; minimal-data diagnostics. | Retain as reversible guardrails only. |
[stderr] | Approval gates | Connected scope, account/sync, multiplayer/safety, commerce, stack/vendors, support matrix/budgets, content quantities, localisation, audio, and legal/store policy. | Record and obtain approval before selecting policies, services, or production quantities. |
