[stderr] ## Release definition
[stderr] 
[stderr] Deliver an original, small, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG for a
[stderr] responsive public web application and installable PWA. The complete path is one
[stderr] town, one dungeon, onboarding, readable narrative/quests, tutorialized
[stderr] party-based turn-based combat, inventory/progression, save/load/recovery,
[stderr] settings/accessibility, and a short ending.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Requirement handling
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Direct requests define the candidate first-release scope and measurable
[stderr]   outcomes in the canonical brief.
[stderr] - Safe assumptions are temporary guardrails, not service, legal, technology,
[stderr]   content, or vendor commitments.
[stderr] - Deferred roadmap work is not release acceptance work.
[stderr] - Connected services and commerce remain unresolved because they conflict with
[stderr]   the stated offline single-player product; downstream contracts need human
[stderr]   approval before selecting their architecture or policy.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Originality boundary
[stderr] 
[stderr] The named game is a functional scope reference only. No branding, copy, assets,
[stderr] layouts, interaction choreography, or other protected expression may be copied.
[stderr] All content, presentation, mechanics expression, and player interfaces must be
[stderr] independently designed.
