[stderr] -## Domain vocabulary
[stderr] +## Domain vocabulary and state ownership
[stderr]  
[stderr] -| Term | Meaning and rule |
[stderr] +| Term | Meaning / owner |
[stderr]  | --- | --- |
[stderr] -| Campaign | The one authored town-to-dungeon story path, including completion state. |
[stderr] -| Session | In-memory play between launch/resume and exit; it is never proof that progress is saved. |
[stderr] -| Save slot | A named local persisted snapshot plus version/checksum metadata and a confirmed timestamp. |
[stderr] -| Checkpoint | An authored safe restoration point. Autosave creates only at approved checkpoints or other non-destructive boundaries. |
[stderr] -| Party member | A controllable combatant. Release one may have a small authored party; its number is a content decision, not a feature dependency. |
[stderr] -| Encounter | A bounded turn-based battle instantiated from authored enemy and scene data. |
[stderr] -| Turn | One legal action selection and resolution cycle; no real-time speed is required. |
[stderr] -| Quest | An authored objective with prerequisites, state, reward, and completion consequence. |
[stderr] -| Item | An authored inventory object; stack/use/equipment behavior is explicit in its definition. |
[stderr] -| Content pack | Versioned original maps, dialogue, quests, encounters, items, art, audio and localisation keys delivered with a release. |
[stderr] -| Confirmed save | A snapshot reported written and integrity-checked by the persistence layer. |
[stderr] -| Recovery record | Minimal diagnostic context for an interrupted session or failed save; it is not a replacement for a confirmed save. |
[stderr] +| Campaign | The fixed first-release sequence from new game through ending; owns completion state. |
[stderr] +| Scene | One authored playable location: town or dungeon; owns exits, encounter zones, and presentation references. |
[stderr] +| Quest | Authored objective and state machine that gates campaign progress and rewards. |
[stderr] +| Party | Player-controlled combat group; owns members' current combat-ready values and progression. Exact party size is an authoring decision. |
[stderr] +| Encounter | A combat instance created from an authored encounter definition; never persists mid-turn. |
[stderr] +| Item | Authored definition; an inventory stack/reference is the player-owned instance/count. |
[stderr] +| Save snapshot | Versioned, validated, atomic representation of durable player state at a safe boundary. |
[stderr] +| Checkpoint | Authored or system-selected safe snapshot point; it is not a promise to restore arbitrary moment-to-moment state. |
[stderr] +| Content package | Versioned original scenes, dialogue, quests, encounters, items, translations, and audiovisual assets delivered together. |
