[stderr] -Cross-domain invariants:
[stderr] +**Cross-domain invariants and lifecycle boundaries**
[stderr]  
[stderr] -1. A quest transition, inventory reward, defeated encounter, route unlock, and ending flag become durable together only in a confirmed save/checkpoint; a failed write leaves the previous confirmed save loadable.
[stderr] -2. An encounter consumes only an immutable authored definition and a session instance. Its reward is granted exactly once, recorded with the encounter/quest state, and cannot reappear after load.
[stderr] -3. Content identifiers, localisation keys, and save schema versions are stable within a released content pack. A load either migrates explicitly or fails safely without overwriting the source slot.
[stderr] -4. Settings and accessibility preferences apply to menus and gameplay but cannot change combat legality, quest completion, or save integrity.
[stderr] -5. Offline play depends only on local approved assets and local storage. Connected/account features, if later approved, cannot make the campaign, a save, or recovery unavailable.
[stderr] -6. Refresh/install/cache transitions occur only at shell-controlled safe boundaries; active combat and unsaved state are preserved or the player is warned before leaving.
[stderr] -
[stderr] -Lifecycle boundaries are: authored data becomes immutable release content at packaging; content plus user choices becomes ephemeral session state at launch; only validated checkpoints cross into persisted save state; a loaded save becomes a new session only after schema/content validation; obsolete caches and deleted saves are removed only after their respective safety/confirmation rules.
