[stderr] -## Product boundary
[stderr] +## Product outcome and personas
[stderr]  
[stderr] -Mock Fantasy Quest 4 is an original, small, single-player 2D fantasy RPG for a responsive public web application and installable PWA. A player explores one town and one dungeon, completes a short quest chain, wins turn-based encounters, manages a small inventory, saves or resumes safely, and reaches a short ending. The first release is useful without sign-in, remote sync, multiplayer, purchases, live operations, analytics, seasonal content, or player-created content.
[stderr] +The first release is successful when a casual or adult player can start the
[stderr] +original 2D fantasy adventure, complete an understandable first battle, save,
[stderr] +return later without losing confirmed progress, finish the single town and
[stderr] +dungeon story, and reach its short ending offline after installation or a
[stderr] +successful first asset download.
[stderr]  
[stderr] -The reference permits only the broad *party-based turn-based adventure* scope. All names, writing, art, audio, UI, maps, rules expression, and interactions are original.
[stderr] -
[stderr] -## Personas, jobs, and success measures
[stderr] -
[stderr] -| Persona | Job to be done | First-session success | Product obligations |
[stderr] +| Persona | Job to be done | Success signal | Relevant journeys |
[stderr]  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] -| Casual story player | “When I have a short break, let me make clear progress in a friendly fantasy story without needing genre expertise.” | Completes the first battle and can explain how to save. | Clear objective, low-friction controls, readable state, forgiving recovery. |
[stderr] -| Adult returning player | “When I return after an interruption or a long gap, let me safely continue from meaningful progress.” | Resumes a valid save and knows what changed since the last checkpoint. | Explicit save status, deterministic resume, pause, recovery and update messaging. |
[stderr] -| Access-needs player | “When I play with my preferred input and readability settings, let me understand and operate every required action.” | Enables a relevant setting and finishes the tutorial battle. | Keyboard, mouse, touch and gamepad support; captions; readable text; visual controls; no timing-critical required input. |
[stderr] -| Offline or unreliable-network player | “When the network is absent or weak, let me play the installed campaign and protect my progress.” | Starts from cached content and saves locally. | Offline assets, durable local save attempts, clear disconnected state, no required online dependency. |
